A third-party copy of that sample added support for a mods switchboard. That code is
not used here: this version has its own switch support, written from scratch.

This version is a modified version of the original. The changes:
  1. Edits are recorded after they ran, from the tool's own result, not at call time.
  2. The diff has the file's line numbers and context lines.
  3. Nothing is read from disk to record an edit.
  4. A Myers line diff replaces the 400-line LCS table.
  5. The 12-line cap per step is replaced by a scrolling window.
  6. Any of the last turns can be replayed, not only the last.
  7. New views (file view, file list, summary header, side by side, jump to a file).
  8. A filter by file, and copy or save of a patch.
  9. Syntax colours through the engine's diff drawing, following the person's theme.
 10. Shopify file names, and folded diffs for minified, generated and very large changes.
 11. NotebookEdit, and Bash rm, mv, git rm and git mv, binary files, writes held for review.
 12. The step strip is cut around the current step when there are many steps.
 13. State is kept in $.state, and survives a reload of the mod.
 14. Switch file in ~/.claude/claude-mods/, read at event time, with no timer.
 15. A log file, a settings screen, and more /replay words.
 16. TypeScript and JSX in several modules, with tests, instead of one .mjs file.

Each source file that derives from the original says so in its header.
